e $xy$-plane equals $4$ times the square of the distance from that point to the $z$-axis. In other words, the tangent of the angle between any position vector on the surface and the $z$-axis must be equal to\n\n$$\n\\frac{r}{z}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{r}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}}=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{{r}^{2}}{4{r}^{2}}}=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the tangent of this angle can be a positive or negative number, the $z$-coordinate can also be positive or negative.\n\nOn the other hand, $\\theta $ can vary arbitrarily in its domain. \n\nTherefore, our surface is the cone shown below.\n\n![](images/7c/7c8d0cefa5eb8da76f6cba59570670e4078c278c801aeb12344dce3183733149.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399434 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399434 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399434 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399434 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399434 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399434 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399434 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399434 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186399435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399434 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a3e58f04-a3aa-5025-b3f4-1d84092aa5ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399435 #edb/ref 1080 "A cone" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399435 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399435 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dad703c3-2424-5fc7-a7e2-7cdbd0fd3e2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399436 #edb/ref 1080 "A half-plane that passes through the $z$-axis" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399436 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399436 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c30f7111-a28b-57da-8d7e-ebcc59c3fd70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399437 #edb/ref 1080 "A sphere" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592